Parked decision: GitHub Pages or Vercel?
-- The Vercel mirror at https://jdthaler-github-io.vercel.app is staying up
   for now while you decide.  It builds main, not live, so it doubles as a
   preview of whatever has not shipped yet.  Nothing about it lives in this
   repo (no vercel.json, no .vercel/) -- it is the Vercel GitHub App plus a
   linked project, both undone from their own dashboards if you drop it.

   Checked 28 July 2026, and worth knowing before choosing:

   -- Vercel does NOT resolve Git LFS either.  A talk PDF fetched from the
      mirror comes back 132 bytes: the pointer file, exactly as GitHub Pages
      serves it.  So switching hosts would not retire talks_base_url or the
      get-talk-url.html indirection.  If that was the hoped-for win, it is
      not there.
   -- The real upside is the build.  Vercel would run whatever Jekyll you
      tell it to, which is the same escape from the 3.10 pin that moving to
      GitHub Actions would give -- see item #10 in the review.  Choose
      between them on that basis, not on LFS.
   -- The mirror sends no noindex header and has no robots.txt, so it is
      crawlable.  It is not a duplicate-content problem only because every
      page carries <link rel="canonical" href="https://jthaler.net/...">,
      which works because _config.yml sets `url` explicitly.  If you ever
      blank that, the mirror starts competing with the real site in search.
   -- While the GitHub App stays installed, Vercel posts two checks on every
      PR.  Harmless, just noise next to the rake test result.


Carried over from the July 2026 review (docs/review-2026-07.md), which is
now closed.  Full reasoning for each is in that document.

FAQ:
-- Two links to caricesarotti.com files are dead (the site itself is fine,
   these two PDFs are gone).  Was C1 in the review.
-- mhsmustangnews.com article is gone; you said to leave it for now.  Was C2.

External links:
-- 8 dead pages and 3 dead hosts still unfixed from the link scan.  Run
   `rake external` to list them again.  Was C5.

Technical, the only item left from the review (#10):
-- Self-host jQuery and FontAwesome instead of loading them from CDNs.
   Closes three published jQuery CVEs and removes a supply-chain vector.
   Roughly an afternoon.
-- Jekyll 3.10 -> 4.x.  Needs building in GitHub Actions instead of Pages'
   legacy builder, which also retires the live branch as a deploy
   mechanism.  Deliberately deferred until the workflow feels routine.
-- v1.jthaler.net, v2.jthaler.net and wedding.jthaler.net serve self-signed
   certificates, so those 7 links cannot move to https from this repo.
   Needs a real certificate wherever they are hosted.  The only remaining
   http:// links with an owner who can fix them.

Repository:
-- ~1.9 GB of old _site build output is still in git history.  Removing it
   means rewriting history, which breaks every existing clone.  Was the
   second half of #5.
-- _data/mentoring.yml holds contact details for 78 people in a public
   repo, left as-is by your decision.  Was 1b.